## Schedule

- Cadence: <daily | weekly | CRON_EXPRESSION>
- Runner: <scheduled workflow → cloud agent (issue assigned to Copilot) | scheduled workflow → `copilot -p --agent=<ROUTINE_AGENT>` on a macOS runner (required for anything that runs the Simulator; pin the Xcode version)> (kill switch: <HOW_TO_STOP_IT>)

## Output contract

- Pull requests only — never a direct push. Branch: `routine/<ROUTINE_NAME>/<DATE>-<SLUG>`.
- Max <N_FILES> files / <N_LINES> lines per PR; larger findings are split or reported, not shipped.
- Every fix-PR body contains: **what** / **why** / **repro** (for bugs) / **truth table**
  (before/after behavior at the affected call sites, verified on the real system — no mocks).
- A finding the routine cannot fix within contract → an issue/report entry, never a sprawling PR.

## Reporting

- Channel: <SLACK_CHANNEL | ISSUE_THREAD | docs/routines/LOG.md>
- Every run posts: ran-at, what it examined, PRs opened (links), findings skipped, budget used.
- A run that produces nothing still posts ("examined N files, nothing to do") — silence must mean
  broken, not idle.

## Gates

- Automated review on every PR: Copilot code review (add <STRONG_REVIEW_PASS> when the diff
  touches <HIGH_BLAST_RADIUS_PATHS — payments, auth, entitlements/privacy surfaces, cross-repo contracts>).
- Merge: human only. The routine never merges, approves, or dismisses reviews.

## Budget and caps

- Per-run budget: <MAX_MINUTES | MAX_PREMIUM_REQUESTS | MAX_MACOS_RUNNER_MINUTES>.
- Attempt cap: after <N> consecutive failed or empty runs → park, post to the channel, stop
  rescheduling until a human un-parks.
- Completion write is CHECKED: the run's final status update must be verified written; an error on
  that write is a run FAILURE, posted as such (never silently retried into a loop).

## Noise budget

- Target: ≤ 1 noisy PR in <N> (start at 1-in-20 for a new routine; tighten toward 1-in-50).
- Over budget after two tuning passes → retire the routine and record why in `LEARNINGS.md`.

## Tuning log

> Append-only. Every wrong PR gets an entry — patching the charter is the fix, closing the PR is
> just cleanup. (Same shape as a LEARNINGS correction entry.)

- <DATE> — <WHAT_THE_ROUTINE_GOT_WRONG> → <CHARTER/PROMPT_CHANGE_MADE> (<PR_OR_RUN_LINK>)
